<description>
Reverse the colors of the nested rectangular rings while preserving their positions.

Input structure
The grid is made of concentric one-cell-thick rectangular layers.  Every cell
at the same distance from the nearest edge has the same color.

Rule
Find the ordered color sequence from the outermost layer to the innermost
layer, reverse that sequence, and recolor each layer at its original depth
with the corresponding reversed color.

Key insight
The geometry is already correct; only the depth-indexed color sequence of the
nested rings is mirrored from outside to inside.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "monochrome rectangular ring layers s ordered from outermost to innermost",
  "dst": "same ring-layer slots d ordered from outermost to innermost",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) + rank(d) == layer_count - 1",
  "transform": "preserve every layer mask and recolor each d with the color of its matched opposite-depth s"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: NxN square, N even, N=6-14 (i.e. 3-7 concentric layers)
  structure: |
    Concentric 1-cell-thick rectangular rings filling the entire grid.
    Layer depth d = min(row, col, N-1-row, N-1-col). Depths 0..N/2-1.
    Every cell at the same depth has the same color. Innermost layer is 2x2.
  colors: N/2 distinct non-black (1-9) colors, one per layer
  rule: reverse the color sequence from outermost to innermost layer
  output: same geometry, color at depth d becomes color at depth (N/2-1-d)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input==output up to trivial color reversal)
  steps:
    1. pick N from {6,8,10,12,14} (even, 6-14)
    2. sample N/2 distinct colors from 1-9 without replacement
    3. assign color[i] to layer at depth i, filling the NxN grid
    4. output is the same grid with color sequence reversed
```
